From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: extended link metrics answer under the queried address

An Associated STA Link Metrics Response carries two TLVs about one
station: Associated STA Link Metrics (0x96) and Associated STA Extended
Link Metrics (0xC8), the latter with the last downlink and uplink data
rate. For an MLO station the network asks about the MLD address, and
agent_gen_assoc_sta_link_metrics_as() already answers under that address.
agent_gen_assoc_sta_ext_link_metric() did not: it wrote the address of the
link the metrics were read from.

Captured 2026-09-24 on the controller, one response for a backhaul bSTA:
  0x96  sta a6:47:ae:e6:87:23 (MLD, as asked)   rcpi 124
  0xC8  sta a6:47:ae:e6:88:23 (5 GHz link)      last_dl_rate 972000,
                                                last_ul_rate 1080000 kbit/s
The controller keeps the station under its MLD address, so the rates went
to a station it does not track and it showed dl_rate/ul_rate 0 for every
backhaul bSTA while the agent was measuring them.

Split the generator the way the link metrics one was split and answer the
query under the address that was asked about. Callers that report a
station under its own address are unchanged.

--- a/src/agent_tlv.h	2026-09-24 17:46:56.714955655 +0200
+++ b/src/agent_tlv.h	2026-09-24 17:46:56.930789403 +0200
@@ -118,6 +118,9 @@
 		uint8_t *reported_mac);
 int agent_gen_assoc_sta_ext_link_metric(struct agent *a,
 		struct cmdu_buff *frm, struct sta *s, uint8_t *bssid);
+int agent_gen_assoc_sta_ext_link_metric_as(struct agent *a,
+		struct cmdu_buff *frm, struct sta *s, uint8_t *bssid,
+		uint8_t *reported_mac);
 int agent_gen_ap_radio_identifier(struct agent *a,
 		struct cmdu_buff *frm, uint8_t *radio_id);
 int agent_gen_ap_metric_query(struct agent *a, struct cmdu_buff *frm,
--- a/src/agent_tlv.c	2026-09-24 17:46:56.714909289 +0200
+++ b/src/agent_tlv.c	2026-09-24 17:46:56.930727489 +0200
@@ -2046,6 +2046,23 @@
 int agent_gen_assoc_sta_ext_link_metric(struct agent *a,
 		struct cmdu_buff *frm, struct sta *s, uint8_t *bssid)
 {
+	return agent_gen_assoc_sta_ext_link_metric_as(a, frm, s, bssid,
+						      s->macaddr);
+}
+
+/* Report @s's extended metrics under @reported_mac - the same rule as
+ * agent_gen_assoc_sta_link_metrics_as(), and for the same reason. The two
+ * TLVs travel in one response; when the link metrics named the MLD that was
+ * asked about and these named the link, the controller filed the rates under
+ * a station it does not track. Measured 2026-09-24 on the controller: the
+ * Associated STA Extended Link Metrics of a backhaul bSTA carried
+ * last_dl_rate 972000 / last_ul_rate 1080000 kbit/s under its 5 GHz link
+ * address a6:47:ae:e6:88:23, while the controller showed that bSTA
+ * (MLD a6:47:ae:e6:87:23) at dl_rate 0 / ul_rate 0. */
+int agent_gen_assoc_sta_ext_link_metric_as(struct agent *a,
+		struct cmdu_buff *frm, struct sta *s, uint8_t *bssid,
+		uint8_t *reported_mac)
+{
 	int ret, i;
 	int offset = 0;
 	struct tlv *t;
@@ -2057,7 +2074,7 @@
 
 	t->type = MAP_TLV_ASSOCIATED_STA_EXT_LINK_METRICS;
 	data = (struct tlv_sta_ext_link_metric *) t->data;
-	memcpy(data->macaddr, s->macaddr, 6);
+	memcpy(data->macaddr, reported_mac, 6);
 	data->num_bss = 1;
 	offset = sizeof(*data);
 
--- a/src/agent_cmdu.c	2026-09-24 17:46:56.714985570 +0200
+++ b/src/agent_cmdu.c	2026-09-24 17:46:56.930843438 +0200
@@ -517,8 +517,10 @@
 		if (ret)
 			goto error;
 
-		/* Associated STA Extended Link Metrics TLV */
-		ret = agent_gen_assoc_sta_ext_link_metric(a, frm, s, s->bssid);
+		/* Associated STA Extended Link Metrics TLV, under the same
+		 * address as the link metrics above */
+		ret = agent_gen_assoc_sta_ext_link_metric_as(a, frm, s, s->bssid,
+							     query->macaddr);
 		if (ret)
 			goto error;
 	} else {
